 "snapNote": "snap = [wind-up value, contact value] of the right wrist, read from the two poses. In this rig rwx is the te-no-uchi snap (it swings the blade toward its edge, in line with the forearm: bigger = further through the cut); rwz bends the wrist sideways and is used to keep the edge on the cut plane (hasuji) on diagonals; rfy (forearm roll) turns the edge for horizontal and rising cuts. Key the contact with \"ease\": \"snap\", \"drag\": 0 so the wrist arrives with everything else.",
 "timingNote": "frames at 24 fps: anticipation (wind-up incl. a 2-3 frame hang) / snap (wind-up → contact; the feet and hips go in the first half, the blade in the second) / followThrough (contact → finish) / settle (hold with \"settle\": 1 before recovering).",
